{"strongs": "H0319", "word": "אַחֲרִית", "translit": "a.cha.rit", "root": "אחל", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "after-part, end", "definition": "אַחֲרִית 61 noun feminine after-part, end ; — \\ \\ a. of place, only Psalm Eccl 139:9 (late) יָם ׳ א . \\ \\ b. of time, latter part or actual close (according to context), opposed to רֵאשִׁית ; — of year Deut 11:12 of a man's life Num 23:10 ; Prov 5:11 ; Job 8:7 ; Job 42:12 of a people's existence Num 24:20 = final lot Deut 32:20 ; Deut 32:29 ; Jer 12:4 ; Jer 31:17 ; Ps 73:17 a future , i.e. a happy close of life, suggesting sometimes the idea of a posterity, promised to the righteous Prov 23:18 (|| תִּקְוָה hope ) Prov 24:14 ; Jer 29:11 ( וְתִקְוָה ׳ לָתֵת לָכֶם א ), withheld from the wicked Prov 24:20 (|| ׃ נֵר יִדְעָֽח ׃ see below); the end or ultimate issue of a course of action Jer 5:31 ; Prov 14:12 ; Prov 23:32 (of wine, i.e. of indulgence in it) Prov 25:8 ; Isa 46:10 (absolute, but implicitly of a phase of history) Isa 47:7 (of the conduct described v Isa 47:6 b-7 a) Dan 12:8 ; Eccl 7:8 of a prediction = the event Isa 41:22 . בְּאַחֲרִית הַיָּמִים in the end of the days , a prophetic phrase denoting the final period of the history so far as the speaker's perspective reaches; the sense thus varies with the context, but it often = the ideal or Messianic future; Gen 49:1 (of the period of Israel's possession of Canaan) Num 24:14 ; Deut 4:30 (of the period of Israel's return to God after adversity) Deut 31:29 (of the period of Israel's rebellion) Hos 3:5 ; Isa 2:2 ( = Mic 4:1 ) Jer 23:20 (see Graf) = Jer 30:24 ; Jer 48:47 ; Jer 49:39 ; Ezek 38:16 (of the period of Gog's attack upon restored Israel) Dan 2:28 (Aramaic) Dan 10:14 (of the age of Antiochus Epiphanes): compare הַשָּׁנִים ׳ כְּא Ezek 38:8 . \\ \\ c. הַגּוֺיִם ׳ א Jer 50:12 the last, hindermost of the nations (of Babylon), opposed to ראשׁית הגוים Amos 6:1 (Israel) compare Num 24:20 (Amalek) chief of the nations. \\ \\ d. concrete posterity (extension of usage noted above in Prov 24:20 ) Ps 37:37 ; Ps 37:38 ( possibly not more than 'a future' here) Ps 109:13 (|| אַחֵר יִמַּח שְׁמָם בְּדוֺר ) Amos 4:2 ; Amos 9:1 ; Ezek 23:25 (twice in verse) (according to others, in these four passages, remnant, residue ) Dan 11:4 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB342')\">BDB342</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H319')\">H319</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB341')\">BDB341</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB343')\">BDB343</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אַחֲרִית</bdbheb><sub>61</sub> <b>noun feminine</b> <highlightword>after-part, end</highlightword>; — <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> of place, only Psalm <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 139:9\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"139\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"139\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(21,139,9)\">Eccl 139:9</ref> (late) <bdbheb>יָם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>א</bdbheb>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> of time, <highlight>latter part</highlight> or actual <highlight>close</highlight> (according to context), opposed to <bdbheb>רֵאשִׁית</bdbheb>; — of year <ref ref=\"Deut 11:12\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(5,11,12)\">Deut 11:12</ref> of a man's life <ref ref=\"Num 23:10\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(4,23,10)\">Num 23:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 5:11\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(20,5,11)\">Prov 5:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 8:7\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(18,8,7)\">Job 8:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Job 42:12\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"42\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"42\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(18,42,12)\">Job 42:12</ref> of a people's existence <ref ref=\"Num 24:20\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(4,24,20)\">Num 24:20</ref> = <highlight>final lot</highlight> <ref ref=\"Deut 32:20\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,20)\">Deut 32:20</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 32:29\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,29)\">Deut 32:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 12:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,12,4)\">Jer 12:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 31:17\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(24,31,17)\">Jer 31:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 73:17\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"73\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"73\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(19,73,17)\">Ps 73:17</ref> <highlight>a future</highlight>, i.e. a happy close of life, suggesting sometimes the idea of a posterity, promised to the righteous <ref ref=\"Prov 23:18\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(20,23,18)\">Prov 23:18</ref> (|| <bdbheb>תִּקְוָה</bdbheb> <highlight>hope</highlight>) <ref ref=\"Prov 24:14\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(20,24,14)\">Prov 24:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 29:11\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(24,29,11)\">Jer 29:11</ref> (<bdbheb>וְתִקְוָה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>לָתֵת לָכֶם א</bdbheb>), withheld from the wicked <ref ref=\"Prov 24:20\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(20,24,20)\">Prov 24:20</ref> (|| <bdbheb>׃ נֵר יִדְעָֽח ׃</bdbheb> see below); the <highlight>end</highlight> or ultimate <highlight>issue</highlight> of a course of action <ref ref=\"Jer 5:31\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(24,5,31)\">Jer 5:31</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 14:12\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,12)\">Prov 14:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 23:32\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(20,23,32)\">Prov 23:32</ref> (of wine, i.e. of indulgence in it) <ref ref=\"Prov 25:8\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(20,25,8)\">Prov 25:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 46:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,46,10)\">Isa 46:10</ref> (absolute, but implicitly of a phase of history) <ref ref=\"Isa 47:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,47,7)\">Isa 47:7</ref> (of the conduct described v<ref ref=\"Isa 47:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,47,6)\">Isa 47:6</ref> b-7 a) <ref ref=\"Dan 12:8\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(27,12,8)\">Dan 12:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Eccl 7:8\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(21,7,8)\">Eccl 7:8</ref> of a prediction = the <highlight>event</highlight> <ref ref=\"Isa 41:22\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(23,41,22)\">Isa 41:22</ref>. <bdbheb>בְּאַחֲרִית הַיָּמִים</bdbheb> <highlight>in the end of the days</highlight>, a prophetic phrase denoting the final period of the history so far as the speaker's perspective reaches; the sense thus varies with the context, but it often = the ideal or Messianic future; <ref ref=\"Gen 49:1\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(1,49,1)\">Gen 49:1</ref> (of the period of Israel's possession of Canaan) <ref ref=\"Num 24:14\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(4,24,14)\">Num 24:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 4:30\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(5,4,30)\">Deut 4:30</ref> (of the period of Israel's return to God after adversity) <ref ref=\"Deut 31:29\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(5,31,29)\">Deut 31:29</ref> (of the period of Israel's rebellion) <ref ref=\"Hos 3:5\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(28,3,5)\">Hos 3:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 2:2\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(23,2,2)\">Isa 2:2</ref> ( = <ref ref=\"Mic 4:1\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(33,4,1)\">Mic 4:1</ref>) <ref ref=\"Jer 23:20\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(24,23,20)\">Jer 23:20</ref> (see Graf) = <ref ref=\"Jer 30:24\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(24,30,24)\">Jer 30:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 48:47\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"47\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"47\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,47)\">Jer 48:47</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 49:39\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"49\" vBegin=\"39\" cEnd=\"49\" vEnd=\"39\" onclick=\"bcv(24,49,39)\">Jer 49:39</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 38:16\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(26,38,16)\">Ezek 38:16</ref> (of the period of Gog's attack upon restored Israel) <ref ref=\"Dan 2:28\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(27,2,28)\">Dan 2:28</ref> (Aramaic) <ref ref=\"Dan 10:14\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(27,10,14)\">Dan 10:14</ref> (of the age of Antiochus Epiphanes): compare <bdbheb>הַשָּׁנִים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כְּא</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 38:8\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(26,38,8)\">Ezek 38:8</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> <bdbheb>הַגּוֺיִם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>א</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 50:12\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(24,50,12)\">Jer 50:12</ref> the <highlight>last, hindermost</highlight> of the nations (of Babylon), opposed to <bdbheb>ראשׁית הגוים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Amos 6:1\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(30,6,1)\">Amos 6:1</ref> (Israel) compare <ref ref=\"Num 24:20\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(4,24,20)\">Num 24:20</ref> (Amalek) chief of the nations. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> concrete <highlight>posterity</highlight> (extension of usage noted above in <ref ref=\"Prov 24:20\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(20,24,20)\">Prov 24:20</ref>) <ref ref=\"Ps 37:37\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"37\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"37\" onclick=\"bcv(19,37,37)\">Ps 37:37</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 37:38\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(19,37,38)\">Ps 37:38</ref> (<highlight>possibly</highlight> not more than 'a future' here) <ref ref=\"Ps 109:13\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"109\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"109\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(19,109,13)\">Ps 109:13</ref> (|| <bdbheb>אַחֵר יִמַּח שְׁמָם בְּדוֺר</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Amos 4:2\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(30,4,2)\">Amos 4:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Amos 9:1\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(30,9,1)\">Amos 9:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 23:25\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(26,23,25)\">Ezek 23:25</ref> (twice in verse) (according to others, in these four passages, <highlight>remnant, residue</highlight>) <ref ref=\"Dan 11:4\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(27,11,4)\">Dan 11:4</ref>. </p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Eccl 139:9", "book": "ECC", "chapter": 139, "verse": 9}, {"raw": "Deut 11:12", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 11, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Num 23:10", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 23, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Prov 5:11", "book": "PRO", "chapter": 5, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Job 8:7", "book": "JOB", "chapter": 8, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "Job 42:12", "book": "JOB", "chapter": 42, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Num 24:20", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 24, "verse": 20}, {"raw": "Deut 32:20", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 32, "verse": 20}, {"raw": "Deut 32:29", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 32, "verse": 29}, {"raw": "Jer 12:4", "book": "JER", "chapter": 12, "verse": 4}, 